{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/patrioticviews/posts/hyderabad-water-board-dismisses-rumours-of-water-shortagehyderabad-the-hyderabad/1641822041289781/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/patrioticviews/posts/hyderabad-water-board-dismisses-rumours-of-water-shortagehyderabad-the-hyderabad/1641822041289781/","title":"Patriotic Views","description":"Hyderabad Water Board Dismisses Rumours of Water Shortage\n\nHyderabad: The Hyderabad Metropolitan Water Supply and Sewerage Board (HMWSSB) has dismissed rumours claiming that reservoirs supplying...","language":"en","text":"Hyderabad Water Board Dismisses Rumours of Water Shortage\n\nHyderabad: The Hyderabad Metropolitan Water Supply and Sewerage Board (HMWSSB) has dismissed rumours claiming that reservoirs supplying water to Hyderabad would run dry by the end of November due to the El Niño effect.\n\nA fake message circulating on social media claims that water supply across the city could be severely restricted or completely stopped due to falling reservoir levels. The Water Board clarified that these claims are false and that no such official message has been issued.\n\nHMWSSB urged residents not to believe or forward unverified messages circulated in the name of Jalmandali. The Board also appealed to the public to use water responsibly and avoid wastage.\n\nAll reactions:\n\nLike\n\nComment","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":2006.8690549996973,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}